<p>Chicago pays people who know how to work its rhythms. The city packs nearly three million people into dense neighborhoods, pulls in conventions and tourists by the planeload, and throws a brutal winter at everyone who stays. Each of those facts creates paid work. This guide breaks down the best side hustles in Chicago right now: what each one typically pays, what it costs to start, and the local timing that separates a $300 month from a $1,500 one.</p>
<p>Whether you want quick cash between shifts or a second income stream you can build for years, the side gigs in Chicago below are ranked roughly by how fast and reliably they pay.</p>

